register_gate "tests/test_role_feature_contracts.py" "ROLE FEATURE CONTRACT GATE: PASS" "role feature contract graph" "known role-pair files that share a distinctive feature token produce a bounded content-free shared-resource contract, including frontend generic page files that use the nearest stable route segment, while generic tokens, dynamic-only routes, tests/generated paths, unallowlisted roles, and groups above the dampening threshold stay silent" "AI-era no-edge cross-directory coupling often appears as role directories implementing the same feature without imports, such as internal/db/usage.go with internal/server/huma_routes_usage.go, frontend components with matching pages or route-directory index pages, and Tauri commands with matching pages. The role-feature substrate is allowlist-based and token-bounded: it never couples whole directories, emits only path-derived role/feature keys, and caps each key below the resource-hub threshold." 20
